## Backporting

After the `{{TRUNK}}` PR is squash-merged, run `/backport <PR#>`, or by hand:

```bash
git fetch origin
git switch -c backport/X.Y/<slug> origin/release/X.Y
git cherry-pick -x <squash-commit-sha-on-{{TRUNK}}>
```

Open the PR into `release/X.Y` with the original title and `Backport of #N` in the body, and
squash-merge it. Resolve conflicts minimally; if the fix needs real rework for the older
code, write it as its own PR against `release/X.Y`.
{{/IF_RELEASE_BRANCHES}}

## Releasing

Tags follow `{{TAG_PATTERN}}`. Version files: {{VERSION_FILES}}. Changelog:
{{CHANGELOG_FILE}}. {{PUBLISH_STEP}}

{{#IF_RELEASE_BRANCHES}}
### Minor or major release (vX.Y.0) — from `{{TRUNK}}`

1. On `{{TRUNK}}`, run `release-state-update.sh --add-maintenance release/X.Y`, then commit
   `chore(release): vX.Y.0` with the changelog entry, the version bump and the state change.
2. Push an annotated tag `vX.Y.0`.
3. Create the maintenance branch and its label:

   ```bash
   git push origin vX.Y.0^{commit}:refs/heads/release/X.Y
   gh label create "backport:X.Y" --description "Cherry-pick to release/X.Y"
   ```

4. Publish the release notes.

Pre-releases of the next minor are tagged `vX.Y.0-beta.N` from `{{TRUNK}}`.

### Patch release (vX.Y.Z) — from `release/X.Y`

0. **Confirm every backport landed. Do not tag until this is clean.** Every `{{TRUNK}}` PR
   labelled `backport:X.Y` needs a **merged** `Backport of #N` PR into `release/X.Y` (an
   open or closed one does not count). Every fix merged into `{{TRUNK}}` since the last
   `vX.Y.*` tag without the label gets a decision: backport it, or confirm it only fixes
   trunk code. `/releaser` runs this check; `/backport --audit release/X.Y` runs it
   on its own. By hand:

   ```bash
   git fetch origin --tags
   for n in $(gh pr list --state merged --base {{TRUNK}} --label backport:X.Y --limit 500 --json number --jq '.[].number'); do
     [ "$(gh pr list --state merged --base release/X.Y --search "\"Backport of #$n\" in:body" --json number --jq length)" = 0 ] && echo "not backported: #$n"
   done
   since=$(git log -1 --format=%cI "$(git describe --tags --abbrev=0 origin/release/X.Y)")
   gh pr list --state merged --base {{TRUNK}} --search "merged:>=$since -label:\"backport:X.Y\"" \
     --limit 500 --json number,title --jq '.[] | select(.title | test("^fix")) | "#\(.number) \(.title)"'
   ```

1. On `release/X.Y`, commit `chore(release): vX.Y.Z` with the changelog entry and the
   version bump.
2. Push an annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` and publish the release notes.
3. Carry the changelog entry (not the version bump) back to `{{TRUNK}}` in a
   `chore(release): record vX.Y.Z in changelog` PR.

Only the maintenance branches in the support window get patch releases.
{{/IF_RELEASE_BRANCHES}}
{{#IF_TRUNK_ONLY}}
### Every release — from `{{TRUNK}}`

1. On `{{TRUNK}}`, commit `chore(release): vX.Y.Z` with the changelog entry and the version
   bump.
2. Push an annotated tag `vX.Y.Z`.
3. Publish the release notes.
{{/IF_TRUNK_ONLY}}

`/releaser` automates these steps and checks you are on the right branch.

